{"page":"ALG13","gene":"ALG13","accession":"Q9NP73","protein":"UDP-N-acetylglucosamine transferase subunit ALG13","length":1137,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"Q9NP73-1","name":"1","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"No glycosyltransferase or deubiquitinase activity is detected for this potential multifunctional enzyme"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Not able to interact with ALG14 to form an active UDP-N-acetylglucosamine transferase complex"},{"topic":"Caution","text":"Contains 1 OTU domain with intact active sites. However, no deubiquitinase activity is detected in vitro with this domain compared to other isolated OTU domains"}],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000394780.8"],"refseq":["NM_001099922.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001093392.1"],"maneSelect":true},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q9NP73-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q9NP73-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":53.8,"plddt":[[70,2],[90,5],[70,9],[90,1],[70,18],[90,6],[70,15],[90,5],[70,8],[90,10],[70,9],[90,1],[70,5],[90,4],[70,4],[50,2],[0,1],[50,3],[70,19],[50,1],[0,86],[50,1],[70,4],[90,61],[70,2],[90,59],[70,3],[90,31],[70,4],[90,1],[70,2],[90,1],[70,7],[50,3],[0,55],[50,1],[70,5],[90,19],[70,9],[50,7],[0,1],[50,3],[70,10],[50,4],[70,10],[50,4],[70,5],[90,1],[70,18],[50,1],[0,371],[50,4],[70,2],[50,1],[70,2],[50,1],[70,9],[50,1],[70,2],[50,2],[70,1],[50,2],[0,12],[50,16],[70,2],[50,1],[70,1],[50,1],[70,16],[50,4],[0,1],[50,1],[0,138]]}},"features":[{"type":"Region","start":1,"end":125,"description":"Glycosyltransferase activity"},{"type":"Region","start":126,"end":400,"description":"Deubiquitinase activity"},{"type":"Domain","start":231,"end":352,"description":"OTU"},{"type":"Active site","start":239,"end":239,"description":"For deubiquitinase activity"},{"type":"Active site","start":242,"end":242,"description":"Nucleophile; for deubiquitinase activity"},{"type":"Active site","start":345,"end":345,"description":"For deubiquitinase activity"},{"type":"Domain","start":492,"end":552,"description":"Tudor"}],"interfaces":{},"isoforms":[{"accession":"Q9NP73-2","name":"2","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Catalytic subunit of the UDP-N-acetylglucosamine transferase complex that operates in the biosynthetic pathway of dolichol-linked oligosaccharides, the glycan precursors employed in protein asparagine (N)-glycosylation. The assembly of dolichol-linked oligosaccharides begins on the cytosolic side of the endoplasmic reticulum membrane and finishes in its lumen. The sequential addition of sugars to dolichol pyrophosphate produces dolichol-linked oligosaccharides containing fourteen sugars, including two GlcNAcs, nine mannoses and three glucoses. Once assembled, the oligosaccharide is transferred from the lipid to nascent proteins by oligosaccharyltransferases. On the cytoplasmic face of the endoplasmic reticulum, the dimeric ALG13/ALG14 complex catalyzes the second step of dolichol pyrophosphate biosynthesis, transferring a beta1,4-linked N-acetylglucosamine (GlcNAc) from UDP-GlcNAc to GlcNAc-pyrophosphatedolichol (Gn-PDol) to produce N,N'-diacetylchitobiosyl diphosphodolichol. N,N'-diacetylchitobiosyl diphosphodolichol is a substrate for ALG1, the following enzyme in the biosynthetic pathway"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Forms with ALG14 the active heterodimeric UDP-N-acetylglucosamine transferase complex"}],"length":165,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000371979.7"],"refseq":["NM_018466.6"],"refseqProteins":["NP_060936.1"],"maneSelect":false},"segments":[[1,1,127]],"edits":[{"start":128,"end":1137,"original":"RVLTCPGQAKSIASAPGKCQDSAALTSTAFSGLDFGLLSG","replacement":"STLPGLLQSMDLSTLKCYPPGQPEKFSAFLDKVVGLQK","added":38}],"missing":1010,"replaced":0,"novel":38,"foldedAbsent":287,"foldedMissing":287,"features":[[1,273,0],[2,122,0],[3,1,0],[4,1,0],[5,1,0],[6,61,0]],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q9NP73-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q9NP73-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":86.7,"plddt":[[70,1],[90,7],